   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing Hatzoloh EMS Inc. of Monsey to file an\napplication for a real property tax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S5265",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5265-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5265\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to authorizing Hatzoloh EMS Inc. of\nMonsey to file an application for a real property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize Hatzoloh EMS Inc. of Monsey to apply for a real property\ntax exemption for certain property in the Town of Ramapo, county of\nRockland.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the Town of Ramapo, county of Rockland, to accept\nfrom Hatzoloh EMS Inc. of Monsey an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nHatzolah's mission is to save lives, and to prevent, reduce, and treat\ninjuries and illness. Hatzolah provides first-aid and ambulance service\nin Rockland County. They also provide many other important services such\nas searches for missing people, and have plans to provide community\nsafety and first aid training programs. Hatzolah is the largest volun-\nteer Emergency Medical Services and ambulance provider in the United\nStates, with numerous branches serving communities throughout the United\nStates and the world.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
